{"findings":[{"severity":"low","file":"skills/pr-diagrams/scripts/pr-diagrams.sh","line":259,"summary":"`capability` hard-requires GNU `timeout`, so on hosts without it (stock macOS, minimal containers) the `gh --version` probe fails (rc 127, its \"command not found\" message swallowed by 2>/dev/null) and `capability` always prints `branch` with the misleading reason \"gh --version failed\", silently disabling `--attach` for github.com users with gh >= 2.101.","failure_scenario":"macOS user, origin git@github.com:acme/widgets.git, gh 2.101.0 installed, no coreutils on PATH: pre-change the command attached via `gh --version`+`sort -V`; post-change `capability` reports `branch` on every run, so each drawio PR run commits to the shared `pr-diagrams` branch instead of using `gh --attach`, and the stderr reason blames a gh failure that never happened.","fix":"Detect `timeout` availability (e.g. `command -v timeout`) and run the probes without the wrapper when it is missing, or emit a distinct stderr reason naming the missing `timeout` so the degradation is not attributed to gh."}],"verdict":"approve"}
